From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:55:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Keep the pipe clock on when USB
 power-on times out

Since commit f546912bcac6 ("phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Move pipe_clk on/off
to common") the pipe clock is enabled in qmp_combo_com_init() and
disabled in qmp_combo_com_exit(). qmp_combo_usb_power_on() no longer
enables it, but its error path still disables it when the PHY does not
come out of reset. The common block keeps its own reference and drops it
in qmp_combo_com_exit(), either right away (qmp_combo_usb_init()) or
later (the Type-C mode and orientation switches), so the clock is
disabled once more than it was enabled and the clock framework warns
about an unbalanced disable.

Return the error without touching the pipe clock and leave the clock to
the common block.

Fixes: f546912bcac6 ("phy: qcom: qmp-combo: Move pipe_clk on/off to common")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
index 7d0272fdd7b..45d0a805e30 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -4596,15 +4596,10 @@ static int qmp_combo_usb_power_on(struct phy *phy)
 			PHY_INIT_COMPLETE_TIMEOUT);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(qmp->dev, "phy initialization timed-out\n");
-		goto err_disable_pipe_clk;
+		return ret;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
-
-err_disable_pipe_clk:
-	clk_disable_unprepare(qmp->pipe_clk);
-
-	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qmp_combo_usb_power_off(struct phy *phy)
-- 
